160. Intersection of Two Linked Lists

⭐ Core problem

Distance to intersection:

A has 3 nodes before intersection
B has 1 node before intersection

So they are misaligned.

We must align them.

⭐ Genius trick (head switching)

We force both to walk:

A path + B path
B path + A path

So both walk same total distance.

Now they must meet.

⭐ Step by step visual (MOST IMPORTANT)

Lists:

A: 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 5
B:       9 → 4 → 5
Start
a = 1
b = 9
Move
a=2   b=4
a=3   b=5
a=4   b=null
a=5   b=1   ← switched!
a=null b=2
a=9   b=3
a=4   b=4   ← BOOM intersection

They meet.

Because:

👉 Both walked same distance = lenA + lenB


Code:
/**
 * Definition for singly-linked list.
 * public class ListNode {
 *     int val;
 *     ListNode next;
 *     ListNode(int x) {
 *         val = x;
 *         next = null;
 *     }
 * }
 */
public class Solution {
    public ListNode getIntersectionNode(ListNode headA, ListNode headB) {
        ListNode a = headA;
        ListNode b = headB;

        while(a!=b){
            if(a==null){
                a=headB;
            }
            else{
                a=a.next;
            }

            if(b==null){
                b=headA;
            }
            else{
                b=b.next;
            }
        }
        return a;
    }
}
